      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Williamson%2C_New_York",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was founded in 1802, carved out of Sodus, and once stretched far beyond its current borders.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Williamson%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Pultneyville once thrived as a Great Lakes port, keeping its maritime role well into the 19th century even after the Erie Canal opened in 1823.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
